8	2025-03-19 15:21:12	2025-07-30 17:11:38	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	18	recSen51yfCBIVHAp	d3d693d25d837ac0d6fd3421284fd9ccea048bab	All Member Meeting	\N	\N	\N	144	3	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	13	12	0	t	\N	\N	\N	\N
34	2025-03-19 15:21:12	2026-05-18 00:42:44	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	15	recQKkWHMswkAuKOn	ab6c5b7e65ba1c454f603bd7ba3d49a316513d8f	Metals 101: Basic Equipment Clearance	<p class="neonBody">Learn the safe, careful, and clean use of our General Metal Working tools in this three hour intensive.</p>\n\n<p class="neonBody">This class is designed to impart a strong foundation for beginners so that participants can safely develop accurate and efficient work. It focuses on the proper and safe use of metal working equipment like our arbor press, bench and disc grinders, drill press, and vertical metal bandsaw.</p>\n\n<p class="neonBody">Whether you&rsquo;re already a member or choose to become one in the future, taking this class will gain you clearance to use our General Metalworking Equipment independently.</p>	General metal shop	5	76	3	Closed-toed shoes. Long sleeves and hair will need to be pulled back.\n	\N	16+	Learn the safe, careful, and clean use of our General Metal Working tools in this three hour intensive.\nThis class is designed to impart a strong foundation for beginners so that participants can safely develop accurate and efficient work. It focuses on the proper and safe use of metal working equipment like our arbor press, bench and disc grinders, drill press, and vertical metal bandsaw.\nWhether you’re already a member or choose to become one in the future, taking this class will gain you clearance to use our General Metalworking Equipment independently.\n	t	\N	13	12	75.00	t	\N	\N	\N	Metals
45	2025-03-19 15:21:12	2026-05-18 00:42:45	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	22	recVznWHTN6zhWu1W	b503b09ce93f18532bb3fd6180f3c331833e66f0	Plastics 101: Shredder, Dryer, and Injection Molder Clearance	\N	\N	4	136	3,6	Feel free to bring one (1) brown paper-bag worth of CLEAN #5 (PP) and #2 (HDPE) plastic. Fun colors are encouraged!\nClosed-toed shoes. Long sleeves and hair will need to be pulled back.\n	You can choose any project from our library of injection molds!	16+	Turn your plastic trash into something beautiful and new! In this class, we'll walk through the process of recycling used plastic - from grinding, to dehydrating, to injecting. Our focus will be on using the injection molder to turn your shredded plastic waste into something useful, new, and eye-catching. We'll also learn about different types of plastic, how it is (and is not) recycled, and talk about other ways to reduce your plastic use and join the plastics recycling community.\n	t	\N	13	12	75.00	t	https://d2r0txsugik6oi.cloudfront.net/neon/resource/protohaven/images/class_plastic101.jpg	\N	\N	Plastics
35	2025-03-19 15:21:12	2026-05-18 00:42:43	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	29	recmu2aOMpqdmm817	e5d2ce9441467df6bff920c172a94315383e18fb	Laser 114: Custom Wood Boxes (Rabbit Laser Clearance)	<p class="neonBody">Learn the fundamentals of working with small metals in our Jewelry Studio&nbsp;with local artist Richa Gadgil! During this class, you will gain the ability to turn sheet copper or brass and bezel wire into stand-alone jewelry pieces. You will be using our soldering torches and gain familiarity with different soldering techniques in our Jewelry Workshop. You will also gain an understanding of the step-by-step process that goes into making any final jewelry product for your own wardrobe&nbsp;or small business!</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody"><strong>What You Will Create:</strong>&nbsp;A pendant or set of earrings made of copper or brass</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody"><strong>Clearance(s) Earned:</strong>&nbsp;<a class="neon2Link" href="https://protohaven.org/wiki/tools/jewelry/clearance" rel="nofollow">Jewelry Studio</a>, including the Rotary Tool, Pickle, Soldering Torches, Polishing Wheel, Tumbler, Sonic Cleaner, and Misc. Jewelry Tools (such as handsaws)</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody"><strong>What to Bring/Wear:</strong>&nbsp;Closed-toe shoes (no mesh). Long hair must be tied back during operation of certain tools.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody"><strong>Prerequisites:</strong>&nbsp;N/A</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody"><strong>Age Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Open to ages 16+. Class participants that are 12-17 years old must have a parent present at Protohaven for the duration of the class.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody"><strong>Rules &amp; Expectations:</strong>&nbsp;All members, visitors, and class participants are expected to abide by Protohaven rules and guidelines outlined in the&nbsp;<a class="neon2Link" href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Zgr-sqQiZ6Kf32SUrt1gD8vXS9QXz7T04IGVcownmUc/edit?usp=sharing" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Member Guide</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody"><strong>Minimum Enrollment:</strong>&nbsp;2</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody" dir="ltr"><strong>Cancellation Policy:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li aria-level="1" dir="ltr">\r\n\t<p class="neonBody" dir="ltr" role="presentation">Single-session class or workshop</p>\r\n\r\n\t<ul>\r\n\t\t<li aria-level="2" dir="ltr">\r\n\t\t<p class="neonBody" dir="ltr" role="presentation">If canceled 72 hours or more before the scheduled date, the participant will have the option to receive a refund, or have their registration moved to another class or workshop.</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t\t<li aria-level="2" dir="ltr">\r\n\t\t<p class="neonBody" dir="ltr" role="presentation">If canceled within 72 hours of the scheduled date, no refund will be provided, but the participant may choose to have their registration moved to another class or workshop or to receive a credit on their account.</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li aria-level="1" dir="ltr">\r\n\t<p class="neonBody" dir="ltr" role="presentation">Multi-session class or workshop</p>\r\n\r\n\t<ul>\r\n\t\t<li aria-level="2" dir="ltr">\r\n\t\t<p class="neonBody" dir="ltr" role="presentation">If canceled 1 week (7 days) prior to the start date, the participant will have the option to receive a refund or account credit minus a $35 cancellation fee, or to have their registration moved to another multi-session class or workshop, if available.</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t\t<li aria-level="2" dir="ltr">\r\n\t\t<p class="neonBody" dir="ltr" role="presentation">If canceled less than 1 week (7 days) prior to the start date, no refund will be provided, but the participant will receive a credit on their account, minus a $75 cancellation fee.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody" dir="ltr">If a participant is a no-show, no refunds, credits, or transfers (rescheduling) will be given.&nbsp;Please be aware that there are no exceptions to these cancellation policies.&nbsp;<strong>*Classes may be cancelled due to low enrollment.*</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="neonBody">&nbsp;</p>	Jewelry Studio, including the Rotary Tool, Pickle, Soldering Torches, Polishing Wheel, Tumbler, Sonic Cleaner, and Misc. Jewelry Tools (such as handsaws)	4	133	3	Closed-toed shoes (please avoid mesh if possible). No jewelry. Sleeves and hair will need to be pulled back.\n	\N	16+	Learn the fundamentals of working with small metals in our Jewelry Studio! During this class, you will gain the ability to turn sheet copper or brass and bezel wire into stand-alone jewelry pieces. You will be using our soldering torches and gain familiarity with different soldering techniques in our Jewelry Workshop. You will also gain an understanding of the step-by-step process that goes into making any final jewelry product for your own wardrobe or small business!\n	t	\N	13	12	75.00	t	https://d2r0txsugik6oi.cloudfront.net/neon/resource/protohaven/images/class_jewelry101.jpg	\N	1	Laser
58	2025-03-19 15:21:12	2026-05-18 00:42:47	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	usgqm1d1wjuj7zj4	3	recDfgX83pSzVlNqn	b6ecee4df9ef07da80ef2b00317a3c913db76198	Smithing 110: Decorative Hooks (Forge Clearance)	<p class="neonBody">Learn to forge, finesse, and finish steel while crafting a hand forged, custom decorative steel hook in this blacksmithing intro!</p>\n\n<p class="neonBody">You&rsquo;ll learn how to operate a blacksmithing forge using a suite of critical hand tools (like hammers, tongs, and vices) to heat steel; how to flatten, twist, and shape steel at the anvil; and how to finish your work with natural waxes and oils to obtain the blackened patina commonly associated with Blacksmithing. Whether you&rsquo;re already a member or choose to become one in the future, taking this class will gain you clearance to use our Blacksmithing Forge independently.</p>\n\n<h4>Tools we&rsquo;ll cover:</h4>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>2 burner Forge</li>\n\t<li>Anvil</li>\n\t<li>Hammers</li>\n\t<li>Tongs</li>\n\t<li>Vices</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Materials included:</h4>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>1/4&quot; Steel Bar</li>\n\t<li>Wax &amp; Oil Finishes</li>\n</ul>\n	Forge	4	93	3	Closed-toed shoes. Long sleeves and hair will need to be pulled back.\n	Hand-forged decorative hooks	16+	Learn to forge, finesse, and finish steel while crafting a hand forged, custom decorative steel hook in this blacksmithing intro!\nYou’ll learn how to operate a blacksmithing forge using a suite of critical hand tools (like hammers, tongs, and vices) to heat steel; how to flatten, twist, and shape steel at the anvil; and how to finish your work with natural waxes and oils to obtain the blackened patina commonly associated with Blacksmithing. Whether you’re already a member or choose to become one in the future, taking this class will gain you clearance to use our Blacksmithing Forge independently.\n\n	t	\N	13	12.00	0	t	https://d2r0txsugik6oi.cloudfront.net/neon/resource/protohaven/images/class_smithing110.png	\N	\N	Smithing
\.
